# Licensed sound-library material. NEVER COMMIT THESE.
#
# Purchased SFX libraries (Big Fish Audio / Pro Sound Effects and similar)
# grant synchronization rights -- the right to use the audio inside a finished
# production. That covers shipping them inside the game. It does not cover
# redistributing the source files, and a public repo does exactly that. The
# licence is also per-seat and non-transferable, so a file in this tree would
# be handing a copy to everyone who clones.
#
# Drop purchased material in assets/sounds-licensed/ and it stays local. The
# release packer overlays it on top of assets/sounds/, so a build made on a
# machine that owns the library gets the licensed audio while a clean clone
# still builds and runs on the synthesized fallbacks.
src/freight_fate/assets/sounds-licensed/
sound-source/
*.wav
# ...except shipped game assets: looping beds are committed as WAV because
# lossy edges break loop seams (tools/fix_loop_seams.py, 2026-07-24).
!src/freight_fate/assets/sounds/**/*.wav

# Prototype/audition renders (regenerate from sound-test/*.py, all deterministic)
sound-test/*.wav
sound-test/__pycache__/

# Portable save data (lives in the game directory)
saves/

# here.now publish state (contains claimToken write-secret)
.herenow_site.json

# Build-time secrets (ORS_API_KEY for OpenRouteService driving-hgv enrichment).
# Never bundled or read at runtime; sourced only by the route tooling.
.env

# Local API key notes used by asset-generation tooling.
AI API Keys.txt
*API Keys*.txt

# ChatGPT signsheet batch staging (transient)
data/spider/signsheets/batch*/
data/spider/signsheets/*.zip

# local scratch status (not for commit)
STATUS.md

logs/
.cache/

# personal play/test launchers (owner-local, not for commit)
FF*.ps1

# Codebuff desktop app data
.freebuff/

# Windows null device artifact
nul

# Claude Code per-machine state. A shared .claude/settings.json or agent
# definition can still be committed; only the local-only bits are ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
